WEBVTT

00:00:09.967 --> 00:00:10.831
Hi there.

00:00:10.831 --> 00:00:13.711
Welcome to this video
where we are going to learn about

00:00:13.711 --> 00:00:16.703
the attacker's 
perspective in cybersecurity.

00:00:16.943 --> 00:00:20.399
The goal of the video is 
to emphasize the existing risks posed

00:00:20.399 --> 00:00:24.479
by some unfriendly actors,
called attackers in cyberspace.

00:00:25.007 --> 00:00:28.447
In the video, firstly,
we will discuss what the attacker is.

00:00:28.927 --> 00:00:32.079
Then we will distinguish
the common types of attackers

00:00:32.127 --> 00:00:35.199
and examine their motivations
for engaging in malicious,

00:00:35.247 --> 00:00:38.799
deliberately harmful activity
in the digital environment.

00:00:43.951 --> 00:00:45.359
According to the dictionary,

00:00:45.359 --> 00:00:48.479
the adversary is someone 
who opposes or resists.

00:00:48.559 --> 00:00:51.279
It is an enemy or an opponent.

00:00:51.279 --> 00:00:54.959
A more specific term attacker 
identifies someone who carries out

00:00:54.959 --> 00:00:58.511
harmful actions
in the cybersecurity field.

00:00:58.639 --> 00:01:03.231
An attacker is an individual or entity
that causes problems for regular users

00:01:03.231 --> 00:01:07.039
and companies to perform
tasks and duties in the digital space.

00:01:07.759 --> 00:01:11.279
The attacker can be 
a person, group, or organization

00:01:11.311 --> 00:01:14.751
that conducts malicious activities
against digital resources.

00:01:15.519 --> 00:01:18.671
Typically, we refer to such 
a person as an attacker

00:01:18.671 --> 00:01:21.679
due to their aggressive or active pose.

00:01:21.791 --> 00:01:25.391
Cybersecurity professionals
distinguish various types of attackers

00:01:25.471 --> 00:01:28.479
and link them to specific motivations.

00:01:28.511 --> 00:01:31.551
Today, we will learn about
some of the most common types

00:01:31.551 --> 00:01:34.831
you could meet or hear about
when doing your daily activities.

00:01:35.391 --> 00:01:40.879
Insiders, hacktivists, script kiddies,
nation state actors, and cyber criminals.

00:01:45.727 --> 00:01:47.855
Let us start with insiders.

00:01:47.855 --> 00:01:49.567
An insider is someone who knows

00:01:49.567 --> 00:01:53.087
information available within 
a group due to being part of that group.

00:01:53.695 --> 00:01:55.935
We are all insiders of various groups.

00:01:55.935 --> 00:01:58.335
Typically, it is a regular thing.

00:01:58.335 --> 00:02:01.967
However, in cybersecurity,
the concept of an insider threat

00:02:02.015 --> 00:02:03.295
refers to an insider

00:02:03.295 --> 00:02:07.135
who not only possesses knowledge,
but also utilizes it in a manner

00:02:07.135 --> 00:02:11.247
that leads to negative consequences
for the group or specific individuals.

00:02:11.935 --> 00:02:14.287
For example, let us assume that you share

00:02:14.287 --> 00:02:17.295
your password for the gaming 
platform with your best friend.

00:02:17.967 --> 00:02:20.815
The friend wants to impress
some older schoolchildren

00:02:20.815 --> 00:02:23.167
and gives them your password.

00:02:23.167 --> 00:02:26.847
These older children access 
your account and take control of it.

00:02:27.407 --> 00:02:30.095
Your friend is an insider,
but the actions led

00:02:30.095 --> 00:02:33.087
to some negative consequences
from your perspective.

00:02:33.535 --> 00:02:37.007
That is why we should all 
be careful when sharing personal data.

00:02:41.438 --> 00:02:43.886
Another type of attacker is hacktivists.

00:02:43.886 --> 00:02:49.326
The concept of a hacktivist is constructed
from two words: hacker and activist.

00:02:50.078 --> 00:02:54.718
A hacker is a person who knows a lot
about computers and computer systems.

00:02:55.246 --> 00:02:58.926
This person utilizes their 
knowledge and skills to gain access

00:02:58.926 --> 00:03:02.846
to systems, to steal the data 
or disturb those systems.

00:03:03.326 --> 00:03:05.086
It is a cyber hooligan.

00:03:05.086 --> 00:03:09.118
An activist is a person
who stands up for a cause they believe in.

00:03:09.838 --> 00:03:13.198
A hacktivist uses
their hacking skills to send a message,

00:03:13.278 --> 00:03:16.958
usually about something
they perceive as unfair in the world.

00:03:17.646 --> 00:03:23.006
For example, a hacktivist who loves nature
could disrupt the website of a company

00:03:23.006 --> 00:03:25.998
that cuts down trees 
in the forest and sells timber.

00:03:30.798 --> 00:03:33.790
Script kiddies make another 
type of adversary actor.

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:36.990
Script kiddies possess 
some skills and knowledge

00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:40.510
that enable them to break into 
or disturb computer systems.

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:44.350
However, they lack
the necessary knowledge and skills

00:03:44.398 --> 00:03:47.390
to comprehend 
the implications of their actions.

00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:50.510
Typically, script kiddies 
are eager to discover

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:53.918
software and run or test it,
sometimes to show off.

00:03:54.798 --> 00:03:59.358
For example, your friend could use
a specialized application to run at school

00:03:59.390 --> 00:04:02.990
and potentially disrupt
the entire school's computer network.

00:04:03.678 --> 00:04:06.558
If your friend has no idea
how everything is developed

00:04:06.558 --> 00:04:07.598
and why the software

00:04:07.598 --> 00:04:11.918
behaves in a certain way, 
it means we have some script kiddies around.

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:20.702
Cyber criminals are adversary actors
or attackers with larger goals

00:04:20.702 --> 00:04:24.670
than just disrupting the school's
computer network or public services.

00:04:25.342 --> 00:04:27.662
Cyber criminals are highly ambitious

00:04:27.662 --> 00:04:30.670
and seek financial or reputational gain.

00:04:31.182 --> 00:04:34.430
Do you have a supermarket around
where you go from time to time?

00:04:35.102 --> 00:04:38.462
The targets of cyber criminals
could target payment systems,

00:04:38.462 --> 00:04:42.062
cash registers and some 
specialized logistics systems.

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:45.822
Cyber criminals could attempt
to steal data about the credit cards

00:04:45.822 --> 00:04:48.830
used in these systems.

00:04:52.206 --> 00:04:56.094
In the news, you might have heard 
about state sponsored actors.

00:04:56.286 --> 00:04:59.454
It is not a secret that among 
more than 200 countries globally,

00:04:59.454 --> 00:05:03.134
there are alliances and opposing parties.

00:05:04.126 --> 00:05:06.606
Among the alliances,
there are competitions

00:05:06.606 --> 00:05:09.614
in innovations 
and disagreements over values.

00:05:10.014 --> 00:05:12.526
Thus, state sponsor some hacker groups

00:05:12.526 --> 00:05:15.726
to sabotage events
or to engage in espionage,

00:05:15.934 --> 00:05:20.733
aiming to get data or specific knowledge
related to secret information.

00:05:25.405 --> 00:05:27.805
Now you know several types of adversaries

00:05:27.805 --> 00:05:31.005
and their motivation
to perform adversarial actions.

00:05:31.565 --> 00:05:34.045
Could you think of 
one sentence to describe each

00:05:34.045 --> 00:05:37.037
of the adversary actors
listed in the slide?

00:05:37.341 --> 00:05:40.333
Let us take a moment to think.

00:05:43.869 --> 00:05:47.773
Was it enough time to find the 
proper words in trying to distinguish all types?

00:05:48.413 --> 00:05:53.293
One more thing to mention. When your 
computer freezes or your phone stops working.

00:05:53.293 --> 00:05:56.285
It does not mean
that you have been attacked.

00:05:56.493 --> 00:05:59.325
To attribute the incident
to a particular adversary

00:05:59.325 --> 00:06:02.333
an investigation is needed.

00:06:02.461 --> 00:06:04.029
Thank you for watching.

00:06:04.029 --> 00:06:06.957
Do not forget to watch
other videos in our series.